BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queens of Dim Sum - Mooncake Season
DTSTART:20260926T120500
DTEND:20260926T120500
UID:b5d62b755128c6a38f78edd19e7d1b8d@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Featuring Star Doll\, Lena Đĩ Matrix\, Krēme Inakuchi\, Kuy
 a Atay\, and DJ Sumation It&#x27\;s drag brunch but make it Asian\, duhh! 
 🥟🥢 This is Toronto&#x27\;s ONLY dim sum drag brunch serving gag wort
 hy Asian drag queens and kings at Sky Dragon Chinese Restaurant (280 Spadi
 na Avenue) on Saturday September 26. 🥮 It&#x27\;s mooncake season! Come
  CELEBRATE being queer and Asian with joy and laughter\, glamour and style
 . This jam packed show is steaming with Asian drag excellence. Bring your 
 friends\, family\, and loves to celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival with del
 icious dim sum. 🍺 Cash bar only. Seating begins 12pm\, Show starts at 1
 2:30pm Hosted by Star Doll\, with drag performances by:️ 🌟 Star Doll 
 🌟 💥 Lena Đĩ Matrix 💥 🍦 Krēme Inakuchi 🍦 🌹 Kuya Atay 
 🌹 🎶 Music by DJ Sumation 🎶 1 ticket is $45 per person. Each $45 t
 icket includes 1 dim sum dish + fried noodles for the whole table\, and a 
 show full of amazing Asian drag talent. Order tickets by reserving a table
 . Limited tables available that seat 2\, 4\, 5-7\, and 8-10 people. Shared
  Tables for small groups: If you are a small group between 1-5 people and 
 private tables are sold out\, you can buy seats directly at shared tables 
 with the &quot\;Single Seats at Shared Table&quot\; ticket option. *******
 **************************************************************************
 ******** ℹ️ Created by queer Asians\, we strive to create a safer spac
 e for queer and trans people of colour\, plus their allies. 📍 This even
 t takes place on the unceded traditional territory of many nations includi
 ng the Mississaugas of the Credit\, the Anishnabeg\, the Chippewa\, the Ha
 udenosaunee and the Wendat peoples and is now home to many diverse First N
 ations\, Inuit and Métis peoples. We take this time to try to do better w
 ith this small but first step in raising awareness on how we as immigrants
  and descendants of immigrants still benefit from the harms caused by colo
 nialism. We cannot ignore the history of genocide on this land and its imp
 act on Indigenous peoples still continues today. We encourage guests to ta
 ke this opportunity to learn more about this land&#x27\;s history and how 
 they can support Indigenous nations in both small and large ways. ♿️ A
 ccessibility: Accessible entrance to Dragon City Mall is on Dundas St for 
 assistive mobility devices. An elevator goes to the top floor directly to 
 the restaurant. Please let us know if you have any essential accessibility
  needs. 🚽 The washrooms are divided by binary genders (men or women). 
 📸 Photos will be taken at this event and posted on our social media. 
 ‍
LOCATION:Sky Dragon Chinese Restaurant\, 280 Spadina Avenue
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queens-of-dim-sum---mooncake-season-2
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
