BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Orange Shirt Day Community Event
DTSTART:20260929T150000
DTEND:20260929T150000
UID:2dfcdc2d194fc26858122af617f0a74a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Tuesday\, September 29 from 3 to 7 p.m. for an afte
 rnoon of activities\, panel discussions\, Indigenous food\, and an art dis
 play reflecting the ongoing legacy of Orange Shirt Day and the National Da
 y for Truth and Reconciliation (September 30). This all-ages and all-natio
 ns gathering will include a Sacred Fire and opportunities for storytelling
  and learning with Indigenous Traditional Teachers and Knowledge Keepers. 
 Families are encouraged to attend. RSVP is option but preferred: The519.or
 g/OrangeShirtDay. Link in bio. In preparation for the day\, we&#x27\;re al
 so hosting a series of workshops on Tuesdays till September 22\, from 3 to
  5 p.m.: - September 8: Learn how to make recycled paper and embed seeds t
 o create unique\, plantable paper. The paper will be used to decorate the 
 Orange Shirt Day Community Event. - September 15: Reflect on the land\, Tr
 eaties\, and your responsibility\, and craft a personal land acknowledgeme
 nt - September 22: Write your land reflections on seed paper and make your
  intentions bloom. While the workshops are meant to build off each other\,
  folks can still choose to attend the workshops they are interested in. Al
 l events are free to attend. Questions? Email Jess: JDeVittoris@The519.org
 . [Image description: 1 - A collage of photos in an orange filter includin
 g an installation of little shoes\, people sitting in a circle around the 
 Sacred Fire\, and a person looking at the installation. Cut-outs of the In
 digenous medicine wheel and an orange shirt with the words &quot\;Every Ch
 ild Matters&quot\; on it. Text below reads: &quot\;National Day of Truth a
 nd Reconciliation: Orange Shirt Day: Community Event. Tuesday\, September 
 29\, 3 to 7 p.m. at The 519.&quot\; 2 - A list of the workshop series bein
 g offered (same content as above).] ‍
LOCATION:The 519 Community Centre\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/orange-shirt-day-community-event
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Death Salon: Grief Gardening
DTSTART:20260929T190000
DTEND:20260929T190000
UID:40cd6071e9f334c36d15928b27c42d6a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:In times of grief\, many people find that a connection to land
 \, earth\, and the tending of life can help carry us through. It is well e
 stablished that a connection to nature\, no matter how small\, helps impro
 ve our experiences of depression\, anxiety\, and sense of wellbeing. Pulli
 ng from their their personal experiences\, Eli will lead participants in a
  discussion about\; the history of Grief Gardening through various cultura
 l perspectives gardening as a tool for emotional processing and providing 
 a sense of control and purpose creating sites for remembrance tending to a
  relationship with nature to encourage a sense of hope and renewal He will
  also support participants with ideas about how to get started or expand o
 n our grief gardens. Eli (they/he) is a gardener and former landscaper\, w
 etlands restorationist and wildlife biologist currently living on Ohlone l
 and in Oakland. Mutual aid\, covid realism\, disability justice\, queernes
 s and art as well as gardening all help them with the little and big sourc
 es of grief that life brings us. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queer-death-salon-grief-gardening
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
